comments.body:
@dzmat I think the initial implementation of the server and client side requires no remote server (I mean you can simply add a function that submits data for example, add it to each part you want to monitor in qBittorrent) and then you just need a server as a virtual machine that would accept the incoming data.

The final server hardware is Linux, Ubuntu and plenty of resources. (Yeah that is pretty vague, but basically don't worry about CPU, bandwidth or RAM.) I think MySQL would be a fine choice (one locked user/pass/db), or I could even set up a second instance to keep it entirely separate from the forum database. A database per version or something like that could also work.

Once there is any production code (anything that works) and we have a willing contributor - such as yourself - I will give an SSH to a machine for testing. I hope this 'setup' will work...
